 # Changelog
 
 Dated, factual, one line per change. Newest first.
+
+## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block E1 (TRA-feasible targeting, leakage review, calibration, W10 tax morale, agent inputs from data, dashboard fallback)
+- E1: `src/04_models/targeting_model.py` adds two restricted variants with the same outcome, population, split, CV design, seeds and metrics as the survey model: CORE (age, sex, region, urban/rural) and EXTENDED (CORE + mobile money + business ownership / main income source); `config.yaml targeting.feature_obtainability` states for each feature why TRA can or cannot obtain it. Held-out weighted ROC-AUC 0.946 (all survey features), 0.884 (EXTENDED), 0.829 (CORE). Outputs: `variants` block in `targeting_model.json`, `outputs/tables/targeting_variants.csv`.
+- E2: new `src/04_models/leakage_review.py`: 456 retained features about banking, credit, insurance, pensions, formal employment and formal-sector products classified REQUIRES_TIN (1: owns motorised transport for the business), NO_REQUIREMENT (320) or UNCERTAIN (135) with basis and source URL (Tax Administration Act Cap. 438 s. 24 and Third Schedule read verbatim; bank, NSSF, PSSSF, TIRA pages). Formal employment registered for PAYE is kept as a legitimate predictor. Refit without REQUIRES_TIN: AUC 0.946, Entry multiplier 6.2x; sensitivity fit without UNCERTAIN too: AUC 0.939, 5.8x. Review in `targeting_model.json leakage_audit.feature_review` and `outputs/tables/targeting_leakage_review.csv`.
+- E3: predicted levels recalibrated within each age band (intercept shift on the logit scale; ranking unchanged): Entry mean prediction 1.86% -> 0.77% (observed). Top-decile multiplier 6.2x -> 6.5x (95% interval 5.8-7.1x); per 10,000 reached 502 targeted vs 77 random (was 1,151 vs 186). `agent_cells.json` carries the calibrated propensity (`mean_propensity_uncalibrated` beside it). Entry page note updated.
+- E4: Afrobarometer Round 8 Tanzania respondent file downloaded to `data/raw/afrobarometer/` (git-ignored; URL, date, SHA-256, terms and citation in `data/raw/SOURCES.csv`). New `src/03_features/afrobarometer_morale.py` -> `data/processed/afrobarometer_morale.json`, `outputs/tables/tax_morale_components.csv`: weighted percentages with 95% CIs for 14 component indicators (civic duty, trust in the tax authority, acceptability of not paying, perceived avoidance, reciprocity, fiscal exchange), all adults, urban/rural and six age bands, disclosure rule applied. No composite: the 59.8% composite is retired, WVS 61.8% stays removed. Gap recomputed from components.
+- E4: `tax_morale.baseline.trust`, `.social_norm`, `.fairness` are DATA from Afrobarometer (Q41J, Q47D reversed, Q47C: 0.785, 0.535, 0.751); `.simplicity` and `.enforcement` stay ASSUMPTION (no defensible mapping). `src/assumptions.py` resolves DATA entries with `data_file` / `data_path` from the processed file. The morale model moved: baseline compliance 30.6% -> 56.5%, combined 58.2% -> 80.5%, naive sum 78.0% -> 100.2% (effects and weights not recalibrated).
+- E5: new `src/03_features/agent_inputs.py` -> `data/processed/agent_trust_morale.json` (empirical weighted distributions of Q41J trust and Q76e-tan morale per age band x urban/rural, Beta fit published as a check) and `agent_income.json` (ILFS 2024 annual earnings percentiles per age band; self-employment and agricultural income exist; 31.8% of persons 16+ have none and enter with zero income). `economic_model.draw_agent_inputs` replaces the simulated Beta and log-normal draws and the income scale (agent's income rank). Agent-based final compliance 59.7% -> 71.7%; tier year-10 not registered 40.3% -> 28.2%.
+- E6: `config.yaml zones:` (nine NBS TDHS-MIS 2022 zones); zone x activity and national x activity cells added to the two activity files; Mzani wa Kodi falls back region -> zone -> national with a label. Of the 42 suppressed region cells, 40 resolve at zone level and 2 at national level.
+- Dashboard: Entry (calibrated levels and note), Active (labelled fallback), Asset (Afrobarometer components replace the WVS / composite sentence), Enterprise (values and caption).
+- Assumptions register: 180 rows (UNKNOWN 47, ASSUMPTION 56, DATA 15, RETIRED 62, including the retired 59.8% composite, its four assumed weights, the WVS 61.8% and the 28 pp gap); 15 claims still BLOCKED (C041-C053, C062, C079); C008, C054, C055, C069, C078 left the list. `assumption_sensitivity.py` flips boolean switches.
+- Tests: `test_targeting_variants.py`, `test_afrobarometer.py`, `test_agent_inputs.py`, `test_fallback.py` (new); `conftest.py` (Afrobarometer path, light variant grid), `test_assumptions.py`, `test_idempotency.py` updated.
 
 ## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block D (housekeeping, disclosure rule, W6 mobile-money/TIN evidence, W9 real-data targeting model)
 - Housekeeping: every file at the root of `<workspace>\` and the former `_records\` folder moved to `Behavioral\_archive\process_records\` (SHA-256 checked, `D0_1_hash_check.csv`); the records both projects share are copied to `MultiAgent\_archive\process_records\`; the root now holds only `Behavioral\` and `MultiAgent\`; `_archive\` is git-ignored in both. Block reports and `REANALYSIS_PLAN.md` are read from and written to `Behavioral\_archive\process_records\` from now on.
