-C032,PDF p.28 | 4.3 Active Stage: Informal Businesses Outside > Who Are They? | paragraph block 446,"This tracks with the national picture: NBS's 2024 Integrated Labour Force Survey found informality has grown to 94.6% of Tanzania's workforce, up from 92.5% in 2020/21, and that 74.8% of workers are self-employed rather than in paid employment — the large majority of Tanzania's economically active population runs some form of own-account enterprise rather than working for someone else.",94.6%; 92.5%; 74.8%,none,COMPUTED,none (value not in any output). Producer: src\imported\ilfs_loader.py (not wired); export data\external\db_export_ilfs_indicators.csv,RECOMPUTE,W1,ILFS 2024 .sav is in data\raw\ilfs\. These values occur in no output; the DB holds self-employment 27.73% and formal employment 3.68%.,"Informal employment: computed 88.5% (ICLS-17 headline), 94.5% under the NBS-consistent rule; CITED NBS: 94.6% (2024), 92.5% (2020/21). Self-employed: 60.2% (employers + own-account) or 82.7% incl. contributing family workers; NBS ""dependent contractors"" 74.8% is a different ICSE-18 class","CITED (94.6%, 92.5%, 74.8% as NBS figures) + COMPUTED (replacement values)","src/03_features/ilfs_indicators.py -> outputs/stats/ilfs_summary.json (published_cross_check, cited_source)",DECIDED - TEXT TO CHANGE,"Cite NBS (2025) ""The Labour Market: Key Findings from the ILFS 2024"", Figure 3.3 p. 20 (94.6% and the 92.5% 2020/21 bar; the key message calls it Figure 2.3), Table 3.3 p. 16 (74.8% = dependent contractors, not ""self-employed""). 2020/21 figure is CITED, not computed (microdata not held); the 2020/21 Analytical Report (NBS 2022) does not itself state 92.5%.","Block C0.3 decision. MAIN TEXT CITES NBS: informal employment 94.6% (2024) and 92.5% (2020/21) - NBS (2025), The Labour Market: Key Findings from the ILFS 2024, Figure 3.3, p. 20 (CITED). TECHNICAL APPENDIX reports the computed ICLS-17 estimate 88.5% (95% CI 87.4-89.6; employed 15+, ILO_LFS19 = 1, main job) and explains the definition gap: the computed estimate treats a self-employed worker as formal if the enterprise is registered with any authority (Q38A 1-5). The 94.5% from the stricter rule (formal = employees with social security + self-employed with a legal-entity registration, Q38C = 1) is a REPLICATION CHECK of NBS's figure, not attributed to NBS as its method. SELF-EMPLOYMENT: 60.2% (employers + own-account workers) and 82.7% (including contributing family workers), both definitions stated; the 74.8% is dropped (it is NBS's ""dependent contractors"" class, not a self-employed total). EMPLOYMENT BASE: 19th ICLS (ILO_LFS19 = 1), matching NBS's published employment-to-population ratio (computed 68.67% vs 68.7%).",,,,,,,,,,,
